section.p:
Maps, like sequences, are immutable. When you add an entry to a map, you get a new map;
				the original is unchanged. Saxon provides an efficient implementation of maps that
				achieves this without copying the whole map every time an entry is added.

A path expression is a sequence of steps separated by the / or
					// operator. For example, ../@desc selects the
					desc attribute of the parent of the context node.

pre.code:
declare function cx:complex ($real as xs:double, $imag as xs:double)
                 as record(r as xs:double, i as xs:double) {
  map{'r':$real, 'i':$imag}
};

declare function cx:add ($x as record(r as xs:double, i as xs:double),
                         $y as record(r as xs:double, i as xs:double))
                 as record(r as xs:double, i as xs:double) {
  cx:number($x?r + $y?r, $x?i + $y?i)
};

section.p:
